Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix: force outputDataspace in composeSurfaces

Remove the hasWideColorGamut() gate on outputDataspace in
composeSurfaces(). This ensures the GPU always uses the display's
color mode dataspace for client composition, even if
hasWideColorGamut() returns false for any reason.

Without this, when hasWideColorGamut() is false, the outputDataspace
is forced to UNKNOWN, causing the RenderEngine to skip sRGB transfer
function application and use default (BT.601) YUV-to-RGB conversion
for all layers.
---
 services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp | 5 +2/-3
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp
index d0c5803..83859bc 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Output.cpp
@@ -1200,9 +1200,8 @@ std::optional<base::unique_fd> Output::composeSurfaces(
     clientCompositionDisplay.clip = outputState.layerStackSpace.getContent();
     clientCompositionDisplay.orientation =
             ui::Transform::toRotationFlags(outputState.displaySpace.getOrientation());
-    clientCompositionDisplay.outputDataspace = mDisplayColorProfile->hasWideColorGamut()
-            ? outputState.dataspace
-            : ui::Dataspace::UNKNOWN;
+    // Always use the display's dataspace for client composition output
+    clientCompositionDisplay.outputDataspace = outputState.dataspace;
 
     // If we have a valid current display brightness use that, otherwise fall back to the
     // display's max desired
